# MYTHHELM TUI recording scaffold (docs-site-demos, FR-3) — planned, not recorded.
#
# This tape is a placeholder: it drives nothing yet and renders nothing. The
# full FR-3 tape lands as a follow-up now that the TUI slice has shipped; the
# follow-up card is drafted in specs/in-progress/docs-site-demos/handoff.md
# (Task 7 section) for the orchestrator to file via the backlog flow.
#
# Interface the follow-up tape will drive (tui-slice acceptance, all shipped
# in specs/done/tui-slice/): the mission view, responsive layouts down to the
# linear accessible mode, keyboard navigation and the command palette, and the
# signature motion moments. AC-3.2 limits the tape to exactly that covered
# behaviour. AC-3.3 binds the follow-up: the tape shows the TUI's own
# verification status, never pane text as proof.
#
# The follow-up tape keeps the demo tape's contract: header comments declaring
# Binary-Version:/Binary-Commit:/VHS-Version:, a manifest entry in
# docs/demos/manifest.json, and a normalized transcript beside it. Until then
# there is intentionally no manifest entry and no rendered artifact, so the
# recording-honesty checks exempt this scaffold by construction.
